meta {
  name: Unsupported grant type — authorization_code rejected (400)
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: none
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  grant_type: authorization_code
  client_id: {{placerClientId}}
  code: fake-auth-code
  redirect_uri: https://client.example.com/callback
}

docs {
  UMZH Connect is machine-to-machine only — the IG explicitly states: "No openid scope is requested, since these are pure machine-to-machine exchanges with no user identity." (security.md §Client authentication)

  Only the client_credentials grant is appropriate. Attempting authorization_code (which requires a user interaction and a valid code) must be rejected. The code is intentionally fake — the intent is to confirm the grant type itself is rejected, not to obtain a real code.

  This test does not require a client assertion because KC validates the grant type before checking client authentication when the type is structurally invalid or not allowed for the client.
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 400
}
